{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen","id":880344,"title":"Thought about Arms of the Chosen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T12:19:41-07:00","id":880344,"title":"Thought about Arms of the Chosen","content":"It occurred to me today, when reflecting upon the echo-chamber effect of the forums, that I'm not sure if it was ever explicitly stated that Arms of the Chosen will have <b>descriptive rules for how to make your own artifacts and evocations</b>. We've all been assuming that the book will give us some guidelines, but it's possible that this was just extrapolated from &quot;there will be more listed artifacts that you can use as examples to figure out your own&quot;. The latter option is still valid, but no where near as useful as &quot;a definitive how-to guide for making your own artifacts in your games&quot;.<br /> <br /> And example is the Exigent book. We've been explicitly told that we will get rules (a charm matrix is the term they used, like a template) for how to make our own Exigents, not just examples to extrapolate from. That's what I want for artifacts. Maybe I'm overthinking it, but has anyone seen a direct quote as some point to clear this up, or is it possible I'm on to something here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:26:32-07:00","id":880350,"title":"","content":"I can't recall the source, but I think it was explicitly stated that Arms <i>won't </i>have those rules. Makes sense, it's slated as a small supplement, but damn: it's not doing much to sell me. As someone not confident with homebrew, those would have been VERY nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:36:45-07:00","id":880361,"title":"","content":"I mean, I can't envision it taking more than maybe 10 pages, including context and flavor. They're not as big as charm trees, and I imagine it'll be more like guidelines than a structured ruleset, but yeah it would be really nice to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:40:30-07:00","id":880365,"title":"","content":"IDK: I'd want somthing with some depth at least. 'Eyeball it' doesn't really help me. That's the approach I'm taking currently, and... I really have no idea how strong what I'm considering would be. Mostly I'm just taking existing Solar charms and twisting them a bit, which... honestly feels off to me..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:43:06-07:00","id":880368,"title":"","content":"More than anything, I'd just like clarification on whether it's happening or not. It might have just been me, but I was under a <b>strong</b> assumption that the book would support rules for that. That could easily be echo-chamber and extrapolation, but I'd have to be disappointed when the book comes out if I was expecting something else. I can live with just a big book of artifacts (especially if there's like <b><i>a lot</i></b> of them), but I don't want to expect creation rules to find no creation rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:51:13-07:00","id":880376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880350#post880350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't recall the source, but I think it was explicitly stated that Arms <i>won't </i>have those rules. Makes sense, it's slated as a small supplement, but damn: it's not doing much to sell me. As someone not confident with homebrew, those would have been VERY nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always hated the 'vague guidelines' approach, mainly because it does alot to marginalize those of us who do not excel at mechanic-related homebrew. It also means arguments among my players over what fits the vague criteria. (Gods save me from the 2ed artifact level descriptions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:52:16-07:00","id":880378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880376#post880376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always hated the 'vague guidelines' approach, mainly because it does a lot to marginalize those of us who do not excel at mechanic-related homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you rather have vague guidelines or no guidelines and have to peel it apart from examples? Honest question, just judging. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:54:20-07:00","id":880381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880378#post880378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you rather have vague guidelines or no guidelines and have to peel it apart from examples? Honest question, just judging. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Vague guidelines have the virtue of still being some form of guideline. Honestly I would be profoundly disappointed with just examples since I would gladly pay for any clarification to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:56:19-07:00","id":880384,"title":"","content":"I'm a little mixed, because I <i>do </i>rather want to see the dev's take on Warstriders. (Assuming they're not gated behind Artifact N/A) and I can accept that Arms was slated as a short PDF suppliment. I get not including rules, kinda....<br /> <br /> But honestly, I'd have preferred Evocation guidelines over more example artifacts. Exalted's not D&amp;D, I don't play this game for looting! A very large number of my characters are envisoned with a panoply, and it'd b great to have some kind of workable rules I can use to create that weapon.<br /> <br /> And yes, there's always the 'don't pick Evocations' option, but that falls apart when your fellow players feel differently and <i>are </i>willing to use canon artifacts. Why should my solar's blade be inferior to my circlemates just because she picked Volcano Cutter and I wanted a specific custom weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:56:19-07:00","id":880385,"title":"","content":"We already got vague guidelines in the Core, under the magical materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:59:21-07:00","id":880389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880385#post880385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already got vague guidelines in the Core, under the magical materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Those are guidelines for what a given material should be able to do, and what sort of effects IIRC. I found that... not much help in writing Charms. I know I want my White Jade daiklave to knock people back, but... that's all I know. And that goes double if you want an artifact weapon that's not made of one of the main Magical Materials, like Gossamer, or some kind of frozen lightning, or Malfean Iron, or....<br /> <br /> (Actually, has Ex3 explicitly said that only the 5MM work for artifacts? May need to go check that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:59:54-07:00","id":880391,"title":"","content":"We'll probably have to wait until the dragon blooded book to get any clear indication what form their claim to &quot;second best at evocations after solars&quot; takes, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880389#post880389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Actually, has Ex3 explicitly said that only the 5MM work for artifacts? May need to go check that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty much explicitly said the exact opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:03:13-07:00","id":880392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880384#post880384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little mixed, because I <i>do </i>rather want to see the dev's take on Warstriders. (Assuming they're not gated behind Artifact N/A) and I can accept that Arms was slated as a short PDF suppliment. I get not including rules, kinda....<br /> <br /> But honestly, I'd have preferred Evocation guidelines over more example artifacts. Exalted's not D&amp;D, I don't play this game for looting! A very large number of my characters are envisoned with a panoply, and it'd b great to have some kind of workable rules I can use to create that weapon.<br /> <br /> And yes, there's always the 'don't pick Evocations' option, but that falls apart when your fellow players feel differently and <i>are </i>willing to use canon artifacts. Why should my solar's blade be inferior to my circlemates just because she picked Volcano Cutter and I wanted a specific custom weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing, I love looting in Exalted but more panoply is usually a distant second to those sweet aqueduct blueprints or that cure to the flu...<br /> Seriously though I agree, while I can use the forum homebrews with limited competency it would be easier to have something more solid to work with.<br /> Also there is vague guidelines and then there are 'jade is elemental' which is simple to deduce on not helpful on the mechanical side which is what I personally struggle with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:03:23-07:00","id":880393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880391#post880391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll probably have to wait until the dragon blooded book to get any clear indication what form their claim to &quot;second best at evocations after solars&quot; takes, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced of that. I would be very let down if the Arms of the Chosen book only detailed artifacts for Solars. I imagine a lot MORE Solar ones, but I'd expect to see artifacts useable by Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Abyssals, and possibly Liminals in there, since they were noted in the core. I bet we'll never see Exigent examples since they aren't a dedicated power tier, so each one will access them differently, as needed by the GM/player creating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:05:29-07:00","id":880395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880393#post880393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not convinced of that. I would be very let down if the Arms of the Chosen book only detailed artifacts for Solars. I imagine a lot MORE Solar ones, but I'd expect to see artifacts useable by Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Abyssals, and possibly Liminals in there, since they were noted in the core. I bet we'll never see Exigent examples since they aren't a dedicated power tier, so each one will access them differently, as needed by the GM/player creating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was just Solars I am pretty sure that it would be called Arms of the Solars, Arms of the Chosen implies at least most exalts unless they have been stripped of the title of Chosen.<br /> It could also turn out to be an exercise book for Solars who want to really develop their bisceps...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:11:33-07:00","id":880400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880391#post880391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll probably have to wait until the dragon blooded book to get any clear indication what form their claim to &quot;second best at evocations after solars&quot; takes, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's pretty much explicitly said the exact opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Phrases like 'Almost Universally' aren't exactly encouraging, That said, it doesn't <i>explicitly</i> say that other substances are verbotun, just that the 5MM are normal, the most powerful, and you can totally use a hybrid of them to make something more specific!<br /> <br /> Yeah, I do use the 5MM mostly, but damn, it'd be nice to branch off for a change. And with Evocation design rules, I could do that. I could have a gossamer daiklave, and have evocations that come from it being essentially made of dreams. Armour of leaves, or a cello forged of Behemoth bone! That is one thing I actually really like about the Evocations idea.<br /> <br /> But without a system to use to create those cool out there artifacts, it's nothing more than an invitation to homebrew charms! I didn't need an invitation to do that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:12:45-07:00","id":880403,"title":"","content":"According to the 2014-2015 OP publishing brochure:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ex3 Arms of the Chosen \u2013 The definitive tome of artifact weapons and armor for the Exalted.<br /> Arms expands and develops the Evocation system introduced in the core book, by which<br /> the Chosen may derive unique Charms from artifacts. Includes a wide selection of weapons,<br /> armor, and warstriders. 64 pages. PDF/PoD. </div> </div> </div>Now, there are ten artifacts with evocations in the core and they take up about 15 pages. Assuming a similar page count to artifact ratio, I'd bet we'll be getting at least twenty more artifacts.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what &quot;expands and develops&quot; actually means though. It might just explain what Evocations look like for Non-Solars. Or it might be guidelines and advice for building your own. Hard to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:18:01-07:00","id":880406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880400#post880400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Phrases like 'Almost Universally' aren't exactly encouraging, That said, it doesn't <i>explicitly</i> say that other substances are verbotun, just that the 5MM are normal, the most powerful, and you can totally use a hybrid of them to make something more specific!<br /> <br /> Yeah, I do use the 5MM mostly, but damn, it'd be nice to branch off for a change. And with Evocation design rules, I could do that. I could have a gossamer daiklave, and have evocations that come from it being essentially made of dreams. Armour of leaves, or a cello forged of Behemoth bone! That is one thing I actually really like about the Evocations idea.<br /> <br /> But without a system to use to create those cool out there artifacts, it's nothing more than an invitation to homebrew charms! I didn't need an invitation to do that!</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note, Spring Razor was forged from both Green Jade and a Venomous Tooth from a Wood Elemental. It seems like the standard artifact crafting method is &quot;One of the 5MMs + Some other Supernatural Material.&quot; Which doesn't mean it's the only way, just that it seems to be the usual way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:23:59-07:00","id":880412,"title":"","content":"I don't recall seeing the magical materials as specified as &quot;5&quot; anywhere in the 3e core. And frankly, looking at the descriptions in the back, it could easily be 9 MM. The different colors of jade as so distinct and lacking almost anything in common (aside from a favoritism for Dragon-Blooded) in theme, they're basically different metals entirely. I'm not proposing calling it the 9MM, just that maybe it's not a defined number. Maybe that leaves creative space for more/new materials with different themes and different attunement preferences without feeling like you're &quot;breaking canon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:25:31-07:00","id":880413,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a> Well if it doesn't give really huge hints for building Evocations, I hope it at least gives you enough guidelines for you to improve your &quot;How I Make Evocations&quot; advice. Seriously, I can't praise that post enough for helping me get to work on designing artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:26:53-07:00","id":880414,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Adamant. Authochtonia is still a thing so odds are that ain't going nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:31:03-07:00","id":880418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880413#post880413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a> Well if it doesn't give really huge hints for building Evocations, I hope it at least gives you enough guidelines for you to improve your &quot;How I Make Evocations&quot; advice. Seriously, I can't praise that post enough for helping me get to work on designing artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop! My powers don't work if you sing my praises! *points at username*<br /> <br /> But thank you, I'm sure I'll get better with more examples. Like I said, I can be content with just a big book of artifacts with no rules. It was more that I was STRONGLY under the impression (and I'm not sure why) that the book would include a &quot;how to&quot; guide and it just occurred to me that it might not. I don't want to hype that up to my group only to find out I was wrong. It's no fault of the Devs if I misread into it, but I'm hoping to get a clear answer early. Sounds like we're all still up in the air unless Croakamancer is right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:31:57-07:00","id":880419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880406#post880406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a note, Spring Razor was forged from both Green Jade and a Venomous Tooth from a Wood Elemental. It seems like the standard artifact crafting method is &quot;One of the 5MMs + Some other Supernatural Material.&quot; Which doesn't mean it's the only way, just that it seems to be the usual way.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* I appreciate it, and have some hope, I'd just like to destress the five a little further. Spring Razor is Jade and a Dragon Tooth, but it's listed as a Green Jade daiklave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880412#post880412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall seeing the magical materials as specified as &quot;5&quot; anywhere in the 3e core. And frankly, looking at the descriptions in the back, it could easily be 9 MM. The different colors of jade as so distinct and lacking almost anything in common (aside from a favoritism for Dragon-Blooded) in theme, they're basically different metals entirely. I'm not proposing calling it the 9MM, just that maybe it's not a defined number. Maybe that leaves creative space for more/new materials with different themes and different attunement preferences without feeling like you're &quot;breaking canon.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>... Unsung, I'm sorry. You're a much smarter guy than me, and I wish I had your confidence to actually try artifact design<br /> <br /> But... the section on the magical materials is <i>titled </i>'The five magical materials' and talks about the traditional five as a unit. :P Ex3 absolutely still maintains those five things as a point of canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:49:47-07:00","id":880432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880419#post880419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Unsung, I'm sorry. You're a much smarter guy than me, and I wish I had your confidence to actually try artifact design<br /> <br /> But... the section on the magical materials is <i>titled </i>'The five magical materials' and talks about the traditional five as a unit. :P Ex3 absolutely still maintains those five things as a point of canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the compliment, but I've proven many times that I'm not the most observant person. I could have double-checked with a quick Ctrl + F of the PDF, but I didn't. You'll note that's why I almost never make definitive statements and instead phrase things with &quot;As I recall&quot; or &quot;I might be wrong&quot; or even just &quot;I think&quot; which gives me room to be incorrect. Which I am in this case. You're totally right and I appreciate you pointing it out.<br /> <br /> However, after I made my little speech about it, I think I will maintain that it <b>shouldn't</b> be &quot;five magical materials&quot; and should allow for more flexibility by it's stated nature for more types. I like that way better and I don't care HOW catchy &quot;5MM&quot; is to say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:50:54-07:00","id":880434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880419#post880419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... the section on the magical materials is <i>titled </i>'The five magical materials' and talks about the traditional five as a unit. :P Ex3 absolutely still maintains those five things as a point of canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I get what Unsung is getting at. A Red Jade Direlance is going to be very different from a Black Jade Direlance. If you see a Jade Goremaul, you can probably take a stab at what element it favors. The 'Subtypes' of Jade are pretty much distinct enough to warrant their own entries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:55:10-07:00","id":880440,"title":"","content":"It's been confirmed that there will not be any evocation guidelines in Arms of the Chosen. We're getting a whole book full of homebrew guidelines for Exigents which should be just as helpful for evocations as it is for charms, we don't need a second book with a smaller and less useful homebrewing guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:57:48-07:00","id":880443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880440#post880440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that there will not be any evocation guidelines in Arms of the Chosen. We're getting a whole book full of homebrew guidelines for Exigents which should be just as helpful for evocations as it is for charms, we don't need a second book with a smaller and less useful homebrewing guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be valid if not for the heavy use of artifacts and the more problematic fact that the Exigent book is far off, lets be honest artifacts are going to be a heck of a lot more important to most games than Exigents. That is disappointing to hear though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:59:48-07:00","id":880444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880440#post880440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that there will not be any evocation guidelines in Arms of the Chosen. We're getting a whole book full of homebrew guidelines for Exigents which should be just as helpful for evocations as it is for charms, we don't need a second book with a smaller and less useful homebrewing guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the info. May I ask where you heard it from? Was it on these forums or somewhere else? I don't need a link per say, just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:07:22-07:00","id":880452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880432#post880432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate the compliment, but I've proven many times that I'm not the most observant person. I could have double-checked with a quick Ctrl + F of the PDF, but I didn't. You'll note that's why I almost never make definitive statements and instead phrase things with &quot;As I recall&quot; or &quot;I might be wrong&quot; or even just &quot;I think&quot; which gives me room to be incorrect. Which I am in this case. You're totally right and I appreciate you pointing it out.<br /> <br /> However, after I made my little speech about it, I think I will maintain that it <b>shouldn't</b> be &quot;five magical materials&quot; and should allow for more flexibility by it's stated nature for more types. I like that way better and I don't care HOW catchy &quot;5MM&quot; is to say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sorry, I shouldn't have made any kind of deal out if it. I just found the mistake funny but was trying not to be too rude about it.<br /> <br /> And I agree! I feel Exalted is going down a different path, with the section and a lot of artifacts stressing the combination of the existing five/nine. The alloy idea is certianly capable of a lot: I just prefer going a little further off the beaten track in artifact creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880434#post880434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, I get what Unsung is getting at. A Red Jade Direlance is going to be very different from a Black Jade Direlance. If you see a Jade Goremaul, you can probably take a stab at what element it favors. The 'Subtypes' of Jade are pretty much distinct enough to warrant their own entries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I concur with that. The sample artifacts call on a wide variety of the jade colours too, which is nicely demonstrative. I was just talking about the general concept that the Magical Materials are essential for all artifice in Creation, which I'd prefer to downplay to open up artifacts made of stranger stuff a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:11:20-07:00","id":880455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880444#post880444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the info. May I ask where you heard it from? Was it on these forums or somewhere else? I don't need a link per say, just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was somewhere in one of the enormous rpg.net &quot;ask the devs&quot; threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:12:20-07:00","id":880457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880452#post880452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I concur with that. The sample artifacts call on a wide variety of the jade colours too, which is nicely demonstrative. I was just talking about the general concept that the Magical Materials are essential for all artifice in Creation, which I'd prefer to downplay to open up artifacts made of stranger stuff a bit more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if someone tells me that a Solar with a Grand Daiklave made from the tooth of their Lunar's Sea Dragon Bondmate<i>, </i>or the sharpened and modified jaw of a Tyrant Lizard is wrong, <i>I never want to play the game right again</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:12:48-07:00","id":880459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880440#post880440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that there will not be any evocation guidelines in Arms of the Chosen. We're getting a whole book full of homebrew guidelines for Exigents which should be just as helpful for evocations as it is for charms, we don't need a second book with a smaller and less useful homebrewing guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thus the dev's sinister plan to force us into buying the Ponced Up God Blood splat is revealed! Buy or you don't get Evocation rules! :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's not good AFAIC. Artifact rules in Exalted shouldn't require outsourcing to start with, IMO: you should be able to create your own weapon out of Core. Running with that idea though, you want something that's splat neutral, like an artifact book that every Exalt could use. Not to have to buy a hardback you may not personally care for just to be able to create your own artifacts with some degree of balance..<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Exigents book isn't for artifacts, it's just useful for it. I know. I'm just bitter over how this whole bit has been handled. Evocations were talked up as a big plus of Ex3 and in the end.... what we got is something that I can't use. To say that's disappointing is putting it mildly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:30:22-07:00","id":880474,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with putting the Evocation guidelines in Exigents. I don't think the guidelines for creating good Evocations will be very different from the guidelines for creating new Charms in general, so doing them in Arms would likely involve a lot of duplication.<br /> <br /> My hope for Arms is for it to not be too Evocation-focused. I want a big selection of sample Artifacts, and that won't be possible if each one takes up two full pages.<br /> <br /> Also, if I ever buy Evocations I'm probably going to write them myself. So sample Artifacts with Evocations are not terribly useful to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:36:11-07:00","id":880481,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing how they do Warstriders. Because Warstriders are <i>fucking awesome</i> concepts, and I'd like to see them done in a way that makes them worth someone going &quot;Okay, we've got this- Is that a Warstrider? <a href=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/ea2f3b79c459fac32e5668d3fdd48925/tumblr_mhsfgotTU21rn6052o1_500.gif\" target=\"_blank\">NOPE!</a>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:14:13-07:00","id":880552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880459#post880459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And thus the dev's sinister plan to force us into buying the Ponced Up God Blood splat is revealed! Buy or you don't get Evocation rules! :P<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's not good AFAIC. Artifact rules in Exalted shouldn't require outsourcing to start with, IMO: you should be able to create your own weapon out of Core. Running with that idea though, you want something that's splat neutral, like an artifact book that every Exalt could use. Not to have to buy a hardback you may not personally care for just to be able to create your own artifacts with some degree of balance..<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Exigents book isn't for artifacts, it's just useful for it. I know. I'm just bitter over how this whole bit has been handled. Evocations were talked up as a big plus of Ex3 and in the end.... what we got is something that I can't use. To say that's disappointing is putting it mildly.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that an artifact book, should absolutely contain rules for Evocations. There is a silver-lining for the Exigent book beyond Evocations (if you're not interested in Exigents). The Devs promised it'd be a great resource for homebrewing high-Essence charms for existing splats. So while I understand your disappointment about Evocations not being in Arms of the Chosen (and I share your disappointment), the Exigent book might be handy to have for a couple reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:33:40-07:00","id":880568,"title":"","content":"Even if direct structure for the Evocations themselves aren't in the book, I wonder if it will still have some of that idea of point-buy conceits in designing the overall Artifact.<br /> <br /> I would also think the book might at least have some discussion, similar to Oadenol's Codex, rather than just being a disconnected list of weapons and other items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880419#post880419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* I appreciate it, and have some hope, I'd just like to destress the five a little further. Spring Razor is Jade and a Dragon Tooth, but it's listed as a Green Jade daiklave.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exotic ingredients are still necessary to Artifacts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:47:24-07:00","id":880578,"title":"","content":"Rather disappointing that we'll have to wait till Exigents (which could be years) before we get any assistance when it comes to making evocations.... might need to just stay away from artifacts for my games for a few years I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T16:58:32-07:00","id":880583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880568#post880568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if direct structure for the Evocations themselves aren't in the book, I wonder if it will still have some of that idea of point-buy conceits in designing the overall Artifact.<br /> <br /> I would also think the book might at least have some discussion, similar to Oadenol's Codex, rather than just being a disconnected list of weapons and other items.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt we'll see some point-buy to be honest. Mostly for the reasons givein <b>Oadenol's Codex</b> actually in that it's kind of hard to do it to an otherwise &quot;Eyeball it&quot; system consistently and someone can and will break it anyhow.<br /> <br /> I kind of am surprised folks thought there'd be a detailed &quot;Here's how they're made&quot; thing, since I was myself expecting just lots of examples to give grounding for future homebrew.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:22:36-07:00","id":880597,"title":"","content":"Point buy is bad. At least for Exalted homebrew.<br /> <br /> But there are other ways to guide design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:26:00-07:00","id":880598,"title":"","content":"At the very least, the artifacts will give an indication of what powers are appropriate at what level. At that point, reskinning might be a viable option. Personally, I'd like to see some more non-combat Artifacts. And some non-combat artifacts with evocations. Not too fussed about whatever magitech is still around; that can come later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:40:10-07:00","id":880605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880598#post880598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, the artifacts will give an indication of what powers are appropriate at what level. At that point, reskinning might be a viable option. Personally, I'd like to see some more non-combat Artifacts. And some non-combat artifacts with evocations. Not too fussed about whatever magitech is still around; that can come later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, echo chamber cries aside, the Devs have said that while the name &quot;Magitech&quot; may be going away, things like Essence Cannons may still be around. Very rare, but around.<br /> <br /> (Me, I wants me some power armor. Don't care what anybody says, Power Armor will always be welcome at my table if used properly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:52:10-07:00","id":880615,"title":"","content":"That's disappointing to hear about Arms. I've had a lot of ideas for cool artifacts floating around, but after posting one to the forums asking for critique, it became very apparent that I had no idea what I was doing. I was kind of hoping that Arms would give me some more guidelines, as I'm not great at homebrewing but would really like to bring some of my ideas to life. Err fantasy life...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:04:39-07:00","id":880623,"title":"","content":"I think just having more Artifacts at a range of levels and effects probably will in itself do a lot try and figure out what might be good things to balance against.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:05:14-07:00","id":880624,"title":"","content":"If it was me doing the Evocation guidelines I'd divide them by weapon profiles and tags then discuss appropriate and poteentially inappropriate mechanical effects for each of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:51:25-07:00","id":880654,"title":"","content":"In terms of how to build homebrew Evocations, I was already expecting the Exigents' book to be more useful than whatever is on Arms of the Chosen. Same for Martial Arts compared to a possible book full of MAs down the line. I think it would be too much duplicate effort/information otherwise.<br /> <br /> Given the multitude of possible Charm effects likely to appear there, plus guidelines that should be useful for costs, requisites, organizing the trees around themes, creating synergies and so on, I imagine it will be the most useful book on the line for Homebrew. If it can help create an entire Charmset based on a god's themes, a much shorter Evocation tree based on a weapon's themes or Martial Art based on whatever concept should also be helped a lot by it.<br /> <br /> I'm not too concerned with the wait, since it is inevitable that <i>something </i>I want as soon as possible will be several years down the line, and unfortunately I'm only capable of experiencing time linearly XD<br /> <br /> That said, I'm pretty sure we were told somewhere (I think in that long ass Dev Video from the kickstarter) that Exigents was planned to be among the first books on the line, so I think it might be available in only a year or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T19:11:01-07:00","id":880663,"title":"","content":"Exigents is going to be the next splat after DBs. So, sooner rather than later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T19:19:08-07:00","id":880667,"title":"","content":"Still about 5 books out, but yeah, it's relatively early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T19:57:09-07:00","id":880683,"title":"","content":"Maybe it is because I am relatively new to the forums but I do see a bit of a disconnect. No one at my table is really altogether good at homebrew, when we want new mechanics or custom stuff we scour the net for help. Problem with the new artifact system (and arguably 3rd as a whole) is that for all that it gives room for creativity it is also remarkably hostile for those of us that cant intuitively make new charm sets wholesale. I hope that they at least explain how Evocations behave for different Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T21:02:52-07:00","id":880717,"title":"","content":"Not having any Evocation guidelines in Arms seems a bit weird to me; it honestly seemed weird not to have them in the corebook. Evocation creation guidelines were most of the reason I wanted Arms in the first place. I don't mind homebrewing things, but trying to extrapolate the difference between three-, four- and five-dot artifacts by the examples is all but impossible, which is a problem given that a single point's difference is a huge, huge deal when buying or making an artifact. Given the particulars of the evocation system, I'd much rather have guidelines on how to design artifacts from scratch than more artifacts (which is the opposite of the tack I take with antagonists, but with Evocations it's pretty important). It seems weird to put out a book of artifacts and <i>not</i> deal with that, since it's the main missing piece to the artifacts as written. I can wait, but I do hope we get it eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T00:23:53-07:00","id":880785,"title":"","content":"Honestly it might be better to have more sample artifacts than a build-rules guide, depending on the quality of the build rules. The rules in Oadonal's codex were terrible, and amounted to a bunch of word that ended up saying compare it to other artifacts and eyeball it, which was where we were before it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:01:31-07:00","id":880799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880457#post880457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, if someone tells me that a Solar with a Grand Daiklave made from the tooth of their Lunar's Sea Dragon Bondmate<i>, </i>or the sharpened and modified jaw of a Tyrant Lizard is wrong, <i>I never want to play the game right again</i></div> </div> </div> </div>... Hey, Kyman, may I sig this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:54:45-07:00","id":880816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880799#post880799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Hey, Kyman, may I sig this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be the first time someone's sigged me, but go right ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:26:08-07:00","id":880846,"title":"","content":"In terms of the MM's I'm veering away from the 1e and 2e normal approaches of; Solars have Orichalcum, Sidereals have Starmetal ... etc<br /> <br /> Seems that whilst the materials harmonize/work better for the &quot;typically&quot; associated Chosen there's nothing to stop, say, a Dragon-Blood picking up the Soulsteel blade from a defeated Abyssal and using it to go hunting other Anathema. It might not work as well for the DB, but it works to a degree, plus mixing things up opens up all sorts of awesome scenes;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why is that Dynast wielding a colossal blade of gold?&quot;, &quot;Our Dawn seems <i>oddly</i> possessive of that tarnished green-brass mace ...&quot;, &quot;Did you see the blood flow out the wound? The sword drank the blood. That's surely not hamonious with Immaculate teachings ... our Brother is tainted!&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that the Arms book does include some form of Artifact creation guidelines or advice; I've an artifact from a 2e game I want to port over that's an Orichalcum and gossamer alloy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:48:48-07:00","id":880851,"title":"","content":"That's probably true for the dragon blooded. I expect that they'll be about as good with jade as a solar, and notably less so with anything else, but they will still be able to get something out of it. Sidereals, on the other hand, sound like they can <i>only </i>get evocations out of starmetal. Lunars are probably somewhere in between the two with non-moonsilver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:31:13-07:00","id":880871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880846#post880846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why is that Dynast wielding a colossal blade of gold?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Took it off some dirty Anathema after I killed him. It's the best damn trophy <i>ever</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:04:48-07:00","id":880879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880871#post880871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Took it off some dirty Anathema after I killed him. It's the best damn trophy <i>ever</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But you know their abhorrent sorcery and demonic ways lead to defile their achievements. It's eeeeeebil!&quot;<br /> <br /> At least ... that's how my Wyld Hunt might have once looked at it. Not so sure anymore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:31:31-07:00","id":880890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880851#post880851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably true for the dragon blooded. I expect that they'll be about as good with jade as a solar, and notably less so with anything else, but they will still be able to get something out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually assume/prefer that they're almost as good with the other MMs as they are with jade, if not equally good with all MMs. One of their distinctive Things is that they have access to mighty First Age relics, and that doesn't really work if they're kinda sucky at using all the orichalcum loot they got when they killed the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:35:03-07:00","id":880892,"title":"","content":"They buried most of the Orichalcum with the solars. But that's fine because the solars used plenty of jade and other stuff too. So they took the nice stuff they could use properly and sealed the gold stuff that only really works 100% for solars with them so their ghosts didn't hold a grudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:43:22-07:00","id":880897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880443#post880443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be valid if not for the heavy use of artifacts and the more problematic fact that the Exigent book is far off, lets be honest artifacts are going to be a heck of a lot more important to most games than Exigents. That is disappointing to hear though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Exigents were after DB","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:54:38-07:00","id":880904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880897#post880897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Exigents were after DB</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. Exigents are important for homebrew, but DBs are probably the most important not-Solars for the whole game.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:17:54-07:00","id":880954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880904#post880904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DBs <b>ARE</b> the most important not-Solars for the whole game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you.<br /> <br /> I would sooner cut Lunars from the game than Dragon-Blooded. The Terrestrial Exalted are essential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:23:04-07:00","id":880957,"title":"","content":"One of the features I loved about the new approach to MM and artifacts is the alloying idea. Mix properties to get new awesome effects. Like how Volcano cutter has Red and White jade to get molten earth, and Orichalcum to amp up the power. (And yes, it really does have 3 MM in it) Dragon-Blooded weapons can absolutely have Orichalcum in them, because it's a power amplifier among its other attributes. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm fairly confident that the Arms book will at LEAST detail how the different exalts get different things out of certain weapons. Like I imagine it'll discuss what the limits of Sidereal Evocations are compared to Dragon-Blooded. Or Lunars compared to Solars. I'd be VERY shocked if it didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:39:17-07:00","id":881047,"title":"","content":"If Arms doesn't have enough guidelines to customize artifacts, if people are interested, I will put some extra effort into studying the additional artifacts presented in the book and update my &quot;how to&quot; guide to be a little less guessworky. It might help fill the time until the Exigent book. <br /> <br /> I take no offense from people who would rather not homebrew or don't care for my method. But if there's interest, I'll put the work in. It's fun for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:56:12-07:00","id":881061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881047#post881047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Arms doesn't have enough guidelines to customize artifacts, if people are interested, I will put some extra effort into studying the additional artifacts presented in the book and update my &quot;how to&quot; guide to be a little less guessworky. It might help fill the time until the Exigent book. <br /> <br /> I take no offense from people who would rather not homebrew or don't care for my method. But if there's interest, I'll put the work in. It's fun for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sir are awesome, literally the only reason I can design artifacts (no matter how poorly) is because of your guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:59:47-07:00","id":881064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880897#post880897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Exigents were after DB</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... The issue is the next book versus a splat that is charitably a year and a half out (at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:21:13-07:00","id":881211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880954#post880954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed that for you.<br /> <br /> I would sooner cut Lunars from the game than Dragon-Blooded. The Terrestrial Exalted are essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, after all, cutting Lunars from the history of the setting has been proved to work quite well; you just have to look at the previous two editions to see that it still works!<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PEpm8PVCeAo\" data-code=\"PEpm8PVCeAo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PEpm8PVCeAo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:20:51-07:00","id":881262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880440#post880440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been confirmed that there will not be any evocation guidelines in Arms of the Chosen. We're getting a whole book full of homebrew guidelines for Exigents which should be just as helpful for evocations as it is for charms, we don't need a second book with a smaller and less useful homebrewing guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>YAY!<br /> <br /> Another Exalted book that I have absolutely NO DESIRE AT ALL to buy. My wallet thanks you OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:45:25-07:00","id":881273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881064#post881064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm... The issue is the next book versus a splat that is charitably a year and a half out (at least).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was pretty sure the plan was for a splat book roughly every six months, given the timeline last discussed when laying out the spread of books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:06:48-07:00","id":881288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881273#post881273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pretty sure the plan was for a splat book roughly every six months, given the timeline last discussed when laying out the spread of books?</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is the plan, there are 2 supplements between the core and the next splat book. After that, it looks to go &quot;splat/supplement/splat/supplement&quot; more or less. All of that aside from whether they can actually maintain their roll-out schedule, which I WANT to hold hope for, but have fears of. Good or bad books, you can put off the start of it forever, but once it's begun, you have to maintain a steady drip or the line <b>will </b>die. And I <b>don't want it to die</b>.<br /> <br /> Arms needs to move out of 2nd draft SOON.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:50:52-07:00","id":881383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881064#post881064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... The issue is the next book versus a splat that is charitably a year and a half out (at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, the effort to do the corebook was badly miscalculated because basically the same people already produced Exalted books in a very reasonable amount of time and assumed that would just be more of the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:48:49-07:00","id":881402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881262#post881262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YAY!<br /> <br /> Another Exalted book that I have absolutely NO DESIRE AT ALL to buy. My wallet thanks you OP.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are less obnoxious ways to express disinterest in a product. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:29:42-07:00","id":881416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881383#post881383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the effort to do the corebook was badly miscalculated because basically the same people already produced Exalted books in a very reasonable amount of time and assumed that would just be more of the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Miscalculated, as in they were incorrect on the amount of time necessary to get out the product. That does not lend credence to the published time line. At one point, we had a supplement in the pipe for &quot;Spring 2016.&quot; Summer is almost upon us.<br /> <br /> I'd like to be optimistic things will get on track, but there is precious lack of data to support that hope at the moment. I'm waiting to see how long it takes the backer charm pdf to end up on Drive-Thru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:35:10-07:00","id":881419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881416#post881416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Miscalculated, as in they were incorrect on the amount of time necessary to get out the product. That does not lend credence to the published time line. At one point, we had a supplement in the pipe for &quot;Spring 2016.&quot; Summer is almost upon us.<br /> <br /> I'd like to be optimistic things will get on track, but there is precious lack of data to support that hope at the moment. I'm waiting to see how long it takes the backer charm pdf to end up on Drive-Thru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me and my groups are loving the game to pieces and pretty much the only thing I wish is more books, currently. That, and actual openness on the state of the things going on in all actuality. Currently we know jack shit about any of the progress being made on the following products. I'm especially looking forward to Paths of Brigid and it would be really nice to know whats going on with that since it was supposed to be coming out this spring. So far its not even on the monday meeting pipeline, so I'm not really feeling that hopeful about it coming out this year, even tho I so would like to be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10762-asoral","name":"Asoral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:36:39-07:00","id":881421,"title":"","content":"I feel like they're going to focus on the remaining KS related stuff first, like the backer charms and QuickStart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:28:43-07:00","id":881480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881383#post881383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the effort to do the corebook was badly miscalculated because basically the same people already produced Exalted books in a very reasonable amount of time and assumed that would just be more of the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Data thus far indicates pessimism is called for. Calculations can be revisited once future products come out in a timely fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:02:54-07:00","id":881496,"title":"","content":"I would be hesitant to make estimates based on one product in context of Exalted. Turn-around on previous stuff was pretty good. I think Shards had a turn-around of about eight months, for instance. That said, the pipeline at OPP seems pretty constrained in general.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:39:20-07:00","id":881524,"title":"","content":"They seem to have become a lot more perfectionistic lately, or perhaps a lot less constrained by the upper management. If they'd spent years on Shards, maybe they would just have been fired.<br /> <br /> You know, I think this calls for a new thread. I'll go post a topic called Let's Guess The Schedule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T01:47:14-07:00","id":881596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881421#post881421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like they're going to focus on the remaining KS related stuff first, like the backer charms and QuickStart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean the backer charms which are already out of development and in layout? Or the QuickStart that is being worked on by someone who isn't a developer and therefore doesn't require something else to not be worked on for it to be worked on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:47:19-07:00","id":881839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881596#post881596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You mean the backer charms which are already out of development and in layout? Or the QuickStart that is being worked on by someone who isn't a developer and therefore doesn't require something else to not be worked on for it to be worked on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you're right, sorry. I should have provided a list of the remaining stretch goals that are still in their in purview for the KS, as opposed to just two examples.<br /> 1. Charm Cards<br /> 2. Essay Collection<br /> 3. Ready Made characters<br /> <br /> Considering we know nothing about the progress of these three projects, or who is involved in their creation, we don't know where the priority will be assigned in relation to the other books we know of. And considering they still have an obligation to deliver on all of the stretch goals, that they are capable of, to the backers, and considering the charm cards probably can't come out until after the backer charms do, there is at least 1 of the these projects standing in the way. So I wouldn't expect Arms until maybe mid-late Fall, if we're being optimistic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the condescension was a little much. I didn't bring up the stretch goals as a cry that the sky is falling and the game line is dead. I was offering up a perspective that I didn't see other people bring up in relation to Arms' potential release schedule. I'm personally excited for the book and the new Artifacts/Warstriders it will bring!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 05-04-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:59:40-07:00","id":881863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881421#post881421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like they're going to focus on the remaining KS related stuff first, like the backer charms and QuickStart.</div> </div> </div> </div>All indications point to that, yes. Which is a good thing, in my book. People put up a large amount of money to have those products, and they are all late atm.<br /> <br /> And man/hours spent on those projects are man/hours not spent on the other projects on the docket, unless Hate and the Hamster are farming out more stuff than before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:27:23-07:00","id":882027,"title":"","content":"I just have to say that Hate and the Hamster would be a great band name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T15:47:44-07:00","id":882299,"title":"","content":"One thing with the essay book I wonder is how it's managed on OPP's half of things, as I think it's probably not in Holden or John's control quite who's in charge of it until it's contracted by Rich. Might be wrong on that, but also why I don't htink much has moved on them for that.<br /> <br /> StephenLS is on the Quickstart which I do wonder what's the current status of more.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:19:19-07:00","id":882400,"title":"","content":"Charm Cards are, quite possibly, being worked on right now by the person doing the work on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:08:47-07:00","id":882431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882400#post882400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charm Cards are, quite possibly, being worked on right now by the person doing the work on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (That's 10 characters, right?...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:24:10-07:00","id":882445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882027#post882027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have to say that Hate and the Hamster would be a great band name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> Also, hurray Charm Cards!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:34:59-07:00","id":882455,"title":"","content":"Look, honestly, the 'what's happening with X' is almost always going to be answered with 'it's being worked on'. Like, that's the base status for this stuff. It might be in planning stages, it might be in, like, I don't know the selection process if it's outsourced? That bit of 'work' anyway. It might be in the 'drafted but having to sit for a while so that when I shower I am struck by the memory I forgot a vital thing so now I have to go and rewrite it' stage. It might be in the 'waiting for approvals' stage. But all of those are work, y'know? They'll get there, they'll get done, it's okay! I know it's taken a long time to get here, but I very much empathise with the Devs when it comes to 'this isn't a process that is easy to break into chunks for a timeline and having an audience throwing fruit and flowers is unhelpful' thing, as opaque as it is for fans.<br /> <br /> It's mostly that I'm friends with the Devs so we spend a lot of time chilling out on Skype together and talking shit, and I'm part of the project too. I'm not, like, an official voice of things. I just know the Charm Cards are being worked on in a fashion that's easier for people to understand as work (thinking about a project is an important part of it, but doesn't look like work) (real life Lucy is an academic, this plagues me in all my houses - I once had a major theoretical breakthrough while laying in the dark on my five year old's bedroom floor at 8pm, this is difficult to predict in a workflow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T21:44:03-07:00","id":882534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=880957#post880957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the features I loved about the new approach to MM and artifacts is the alloying idea. Mix properties to get new awesome effects. Like how Volcano cutter has Red and White jade to get molten earth, and Orichalcum to amp up the power. (And yes, it really does have 3 MM in it) Dragon-Blooded weapons can absolutely have Orichalcum in them, because it's a power amplifier among its other attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that orichalcum is actually a requirement to make five-dot artifacts. Given that Solars can use any artifact regardless of material, the inclusion of their metal in anything is, from a certain point of view, meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:31:47-07:00","id":882640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=881416#post881416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miscalculated, as in they were incorrect on the amount of time necessary to get out the product. That does not lend credence to the published time line. At one point, we had a supplement in the pipe for &quot;Spring 2016.&quot; Summer is almost upon us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about the published timeline though, I'm talking about the notion of Dragon-Blooded taking another year and a half.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:02:38-07:00","id":882653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882534#post882534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that orichalcum is actually a requirement to make five-dot artifacts. Given that Solars can use any artifact regardless of material, the inclusion of their metal in anything is, from a certain point of view, meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little off topic, but that point just kinda underlines aproblem with Orichalcum at the moment, at least to me. Of the 5MM, Ori seems to have the least definition and associations beyond 'awesomeness'. 3E tries to add more stuff to it as a power enhancer, sorcery and Light buff, but that doesn't really hold much interest to me. Sorcery and power buffs lead to the idea of using Orichalcum alloy, and while light control makes some sense, that's pretty specific. It's personal preference, but I find the other MM more evocative (heh) at the moment.<br /> <br /> First weapon I wanted to make with Evocations was a White Jade Grand Daiklave. I've abandoned that project for now, but will likely return to it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> White Jade will always look cooler in my head than Armour of Ludicrous Bling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:33:56-07:00","id":882854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882534#post882534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that orichalcum is actually a requirement to make five-dot artifacts. Given that Solars can use any artifact regardless of material, the inclusion of their metal in anything is, from a certain point of view, meaningless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't think I suggested it was a requirement for five-dot artifacts? I respect the argument that the material is sort of an arbitrary &quot;makes things better&quot; metal with no mechanical expression, but narratively my brain can understand it and apply it appropriately. By no means do I think a five-dot artifact requires orichalcum to work or even to be awesome. Hell, there's Black Wind which doesn't have any Orichalcum in it, and it's a five-dot artifact. I think the point is how expressive that power is. Again, I agree this is largely narrative and probably going to change from person to person via opinion. But I don't find the material meaningless personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:50:41-07:00","id":882937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882854#post882854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't think I suggested it was a requirement for five-dot artifacts? I respect the argument that the material is sort of an arbitrary &quot;makes things better&quot; metal with no mechanical expression, but narratively my brain can understand it and apply it appropriately. By no means do I think a five-dot artifact requires orichalcum to work or even to be awesome. Hell, there's Black Wind which doesn't have any Orichalcum in it, and it's a five-dot artifact. I think the point is how expressive that power is. Again, I agree this is largely narrative and probably going to change from person to person via opinion. But I don't find the material meaningless personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, perhaps what I should have said was<br /> <br /> &quot;from a certain point of view, <i>unnecessary</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't feel it is completely without narrative meaning or point, but I don't really think orichalcum was a necessary addition to Volcano Cutter in the way that it would have been for a sorcerous phylatery which is otherwise largely a moonsilver shapeshifting sword. Orichalcum is unique in being the &quot;sorcery metal&quot;, whereas jade doesn't need any help in terms of elemental magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:42:26-07:00","id":882995,"title":"","content":"That question concerning Artifact cosmetics makes me wonder...<br /> <br /> Considering that Artifacts (or at least weapons) aren't made from pure magical materials as a matter of course anyway (it's always some kind of steel), as well as the description of orichalcum as the most versatile material, if I'm remembering properly, and the fact that there are gold alloys (which typically consist of more than 60% gold) in basically every colour, how outlandish is the idea that an orichalcum Artifact could have basically any colour one wanted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:36:11-07:00","id":884727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=882995#post882995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That question concerning Artifact cosmetics makes me wonder...<br /> <br /> Considering that Artifacts (or at least weapons) aren't made from pure magical materials as a matter of course anyway (it's always some kind of steel), as well as the description of orichalcum as the most versatile material, if I'm remembering properly, and the fact that there are gold alloys (which typically consist of more than 60% gold) in basically every colour, how outlandish is the idea that an orichalcum Artifact could have basically any colour one wanted?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Twilight designs a golden suit of armour for her Dawn Circlemate*<br /> Dawn: Little ostentatious don't you think?<br /> Twilight: What was I thinking, you're usually so discrete.<br /> Dawn: Tell you what, throw a little hot-rod red in there.<br /> Twilight: Yes, that should help you keep a low profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:34:29-07:00","id":897958,"title":"","content":"Having just finished listening to the podcast interview with John and Holden, it appears that Arms of the Chosen WILL have &quot;more guidance and support for homebrewers than possibly any supplement ever before in Exalted&quot; if I'm quoting that correctly. No idea what extent that is, but that's a very different direction than has been suggested earlier in this thread. So yay!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:38:28-07:00","id":897963,"title":"","content":"correct indeed, I remember the podcast, from my understanding they are going to explain how they make evocations, artifacts and probably even charms, since it looks like the backer charms are rolled into arms of the chosen book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:43:18-07:00","id":897973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=897963#post897963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...since it looks like the backer charms are rolled into arms of the chosen book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get that last bit out of what they said, at all. I believe it's still a separate file. I could be wrong though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:57:37-07:00","id":897995,"title":"","content":"Eh. I'm waiting to see just what this counts as. With a statememnt that generic... well, if we do get advice, I'll be happy, but ATM, I'm expecting your guide to be more useful, Unsung. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:03:01-07:00","id":898003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=897958#post897958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just finished listening to the podcast interview with John and Holden, it appears that Arms of the Chosen WILL have &quot;more guidance and support for homebrewers than possibly any supplement ever before in Exalted&quot; if I'm quoting that correctly. No idea what extent that is, but that's a very different direction than has been suggested earlier in this thread. So yay!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I to just got done listening to the Podcast, killing time during the bus ride my Sociology final, and immediately though of you when the Devs made that statement about Arms of the Chosen. I'm so glad we are getting more help. I want to say that your tutorial is immensely helpful, however I am very glad we are getting more guidelines for homebrew of Artifacts and Evocations in Arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:08:57-07:00","id":898010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=897958#post897958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just finished listening to the podcast interview with John and Holden, it appears that Arms of the Chosen WILL have &quot;more guidance and support for homebrewers than possibly any supplement ever before in Exalted&quot; if I'm quoting that correctly. No idea what extent that is, but that's a very different direction than has been suggested earlier in this thread. So yay!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yaaay! /kermit<br /> <br /> Or rather: curse you OP for taking more of my hard earned cash! *shakes fist*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T03:11:36-07:00","id":1316048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=898010#post898010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yaaay! /kermit<br /> <br /> Or rather: curse you OP for taking more of my hard earned cash! *shakes fist*</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... that didn't age well did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T06:55:01-07:00","id":1316066,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Arms is a great book, but not for that.<br /> <br /> To be fair, it was two years before; a lot can change in that time.<br /> <br /> Also, tbh, I think Holden and Morke sometimes rather exaggerated what they'd be able to produce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T07:24:31-07:00","id":1316070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316066#post1316066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, tbh, I think Holden and Morke sometimes rather exaggerated what they'd be able to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exaggerated or over-estimated? There's a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T07:55:24-07:00","id":1316076,"title":"","content":"A fair point, and I don't know.<br /> Certainly, I think they tried their best to, say, produce martial arts techniques, but found it didn't work. And I could well see that you'd go &quot;oh, we'll put in loads of advice for making evocations in Arms of the Chosen&quot; and then not really be able to.* I know this is why they changed the evocation system a couple of times.<br /> *Though this may also have been a decision by the new Devs.<br /> <br /> And certainly, I'm sure they didn't know it would take them so long to produce that massive Core Book. That was probably an issue with neither of them having developed a book before, only having worked as writers. So probably over-estimation.<br /> <br /> But they did have a habit (Morke more than Holden) of replying to every query about whether there'd be much material on such-and-such with the response of &quot;yeah, we're going to do it really well, you'll be amazed by how brilliant it is&quot; which left me thinking that it was entirely unrealistic for any writer to do all the things they claimed they'd do. Whereas Vance sometimes replies with &quot;yeah, we don't have any plans to do that for now, sorry&quot; and if you listen to Minton's podcast interviews, he, to my surprise, doesn't tend to say &quot;this work I did was amazing and you should all buy it&quot; or &quot;we're next going to make this amazing and brilliant thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe this was Holden and Vance just being supremely over-confident. But, as I said, I did find some of the stuff they claimed they'd do a little unbelievable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T08:03:40-07:00","id":1316077,"title":"","content":"Well, since we just go into this well of necromancy, what would be you people's assessment of the end product?<br /> What did it deliver, where did it fail to reach its promise, etc...<br /> Getting a bit of a late post-fact analysis would be nice, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T10:05:44-07:00","id":1316100,"title":"","content":"I think it's an extremely good book, mechanically and in fluff, of weapons, armour, warstriders, and a few other bits and bobs. There's some really cool items in there. I love the mace with a necromancer who lives inside, the sword which is also a weaving distaff, the Evagelion-Warstrider, the sword with a slowly waking demon eye that petrifies people, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> It was also a big improvement from the Core in the art. The art is way better in Arms, and I imagine the response to that is why the artists who worked on it have been used again, whereas quite a lot of those in the Core book have not (I think some have).<br /> <br /> However... as an early game supplement, I didn't find it all that useful. At that point, all I had was the Core (and Miracles)... yes, it was nice to have a few extra options for my Solar PCs, but what I really needed was rules for non-Solar NPCs. It's the lack of those that was one reason I stopped running 3rd ed. In fact, I think, despite how much I think some of the stuff in Arms is cool, only two artefacts from it has actually been used by any of us (I made a warstrider pilot, and the Wyld Hunt used a Warstrider) and both have only ever been used in one fight each.<br /> <br /> I know that 2nd ed did the same, with Wonders of the Lost Age as one of the first books, and then another artefact book not all that long afterwards, which I assume was why they did that first. (And I also don't criticise Vance and Minton for this, as I think it had already been planned and started when they took over). But honestly, I'd rather that, having produced the Core, they'd have then just got straight on with Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> Now that I have Dragonblood and Lunars, the two things I most desperately needed, I think I might be able to get some use out of Arms. I'm going to give some antagonists some of the artefacts (but I wouldn't have been able to do that when it came out, as there weren't really any rules for their ordinary charms). I'd still swap it for a sorcery book, or finished editions of Adversaries+Hundred Devils, or a third splat-book (that's not Abyssals).<br /> <br /> But as negative as that sounds, I think it is actually a very good book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T10:32:18-07:00","id":1316106,"title":"","content":"I like it for the artifacts with evocations so I don't have to create a whole bunch for my players or NPCs. If anything, there are too few of them imo. As for artifact creation rules, the book i useless and says not much more than what we already had in Core. All in all a good book for the artifacts with evocations. I would even say it greatly needed book (because artifacts and evocations) for any Exalted GM, but I don't know if I would say that it is a very good book. It should have been a hundred pages more I would say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T10:42:07-07:00","id":1316115,"title":"","content":"I think it was an excellent book that has helped me make a ton of artifacts, and I think that for the first book Vance and Eric published, it was exceptional. Even with Holden and Hatewheel essentially taking all their work and burning it, and at times talking about how awesome their drafts that no one will ever get to see were, I think for Vance and Eric having to take over in the middle of the books publishing and do the whole thing super fast, it was fantastic.<br /> <br /> It might be unfair to say it, but I think if Eric and Vance didn't take over, we'd still be waiting on Arms, or barely past it, and I really doubt it would look that different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T05:51:04-07:00","id":1316419,"title":"","content":"The Ask the Devs thread has been one in which people have had a means of consistently asking a developer for how they develop a Charm, and Vance has generally given the advice that it has to be designed by feel. That particularly goes for elements such as the kind of play experience it will create.<br /> <br /> I do expect the advice in Exigents to be more in depth, but still ultimately come down to that. I don't think there'll be some kind of formula to precisely determine all of the factors behind a Charm.<br /> <br /> I find that some kind of formula is what people unrealistically wanted out of Arms, and suspect that Exigents will also frustrate that expectation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T07:12:30-07:00","id":1316424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316419#post1316419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ask the Devs thread has been one in which people have had a means of consistently asking a developer for how they develop a Charm, and Vance has generally given the advice that it has to be designed by feel. That particularly goes for elements such as the kind of play experience it will create.<br /> <br /> I do expect the advice in Exigents to be more in depth, but still ultimately come down to that. I don't think there'll be some kind of formula to precisely determine all of the factors behind a Charm.<br /> <br /> I find that some kind of formula is what people unrealistically wanted out of Arms, and suspect that Exigents will also frustrate that expectation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, i guess it will always be a matter of rough benchmarks and ST &amp; player group interpretation what fits or not a certain power style or power scale when developing new charms or whole charm trees dynamics.<br /> <br /> Me, i struck early on upon the idea of using 3rd ed's Artifacts &amp; Evocations system as a basis to adapt god-bloods and the balancing mess that was Heritage and overall it has been a quite productive exercise in almost-charm creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T10:50:49-07:00","id":1316453,"title":"","content":"When game systems like Mutants and Masterminds, Wild Talents and the like exist for the sole purpose of letting people create bespoke powers, I don't think it's unrealistic to expect a little more advice than &quot;eyeball it&quot;. Presumably the writers have guidance on how to develop charms, just give us that. Heck, 2nd ed had guidance on mote costs for custom powers in the Core, and Wonders and RoGD had guidance. Even general advice around dicetricks would be welcome (what is reroll-6s worth, what should be the Essence minimum? What about double-9s?).<br /> <br /> If it's not in Exigents then I'm happy to number crunch the Solar charms and work back from there. But (as critical of 3rd ed as I am sometimes) I genuinely don't believe that the devs have no guidance for the writers beyond &quot;eyeball it&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=4tIk-vUtLBs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=4tIk-vUtLBs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=4tIk-vUtLBs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=4tIk-vUtLBs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T11:16:42-07:00","id":1316459,"title":"","content":"There's more options on the table than just &quot;exacting formulae for every possible factor&quot; and &quot;just eyeball it,&quot; though. Just because Isator doesn't believe it will be the former doesn't mean it <i>has</i> to be the latter..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-04-2019, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T12:06:20-07:00","id":1316467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316453#post1316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When game systems like Mutants and Masterminds, Wild Talents and the like exist for the sole purpose of letting people create bespoke powers, I don't think it's unrealistic to expect a little more advice than &quot;eyeball it&quot;. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is designed around striaght-up different design philosophy than thsoe games though. There isn't meant to be a generic energy bolt that you reskin to fit Solars, Dragon-Blooded, sorcery, or an artifact. Part of the game's sytem design is to allow more than superficial differences between such effects, and we see that a bit in the artifacts presented so far this edition, with farily diverse effectst hat often would be all custom in some systems like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316453#post1316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Presumably the writers have guidance on how to develop charms, just give us that. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Evocation guidelines in Arms is based on what Robert Vance did give to writers for developing them. In effect, they <i>did</i> give us those. Besides thsoe, all Charms in WFHW and FatG have been written by hima s well, so if anything there aren't notes to be have given. A lot of the details/notes/thoughts etc. are what exactly Exigents is going to be for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316453#post1316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Heck, 2nd ed had guidance on mote costs for custom powers in the Core,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly in the sense of &quot;not X Charm but cheaper&quot; is all it gave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316453#post1316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and Wonders and RoGD had guidance. Even general advice around dicetricks would be welcome (what is reroll-6s worth, what should be the Essence minimum? What about double-9s?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonders doesn't have anything to my memory at all on customization, just was a box of stuff. RoGD had a lot of spirit Charms with formulas, but notably a lot of them that folks noticed were the sort of things you break the game over its back if you followed to the strict reading. I also am of an opinion spirit write-ups before RoGD tended to actually be straight-up better than those after, as the generic Charm name list wasn'ta s useful as you know, the Great Forks gods havinga ctual cool widgets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316453#post1316453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... If it's not in Exigents then I'm happy to number crunch the Solar charms and work back from there. But (as critical of 3rd ed as I am sometimes) I genuinely don't believe that the devs have no guidance for the writers beyond &quot;eyeball it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents to my understanding is going to actually have full essays on this sort of stuff, including the traits you build Charms on, keeping things coherent, and all that. Again, a bit of a thing to note is that besides the aformentioend stuff we actually have gotten, there isn't much notes to give to writers as only one guy has been doing most of the writing in this regard.<br /> <br /> I add that I actually thought the advice in Arms was actually pretty good, and it did a good job for me on figuring out custom Artifacts. We have a lot of examples to work with, ideas of how these might grow, and what you can expect for each dot level and materials. That's most of what we need until we get some in-depth widget box, which again, is what Exigents is in part meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T12:07:34-07:00","id":1316468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316459#post1316459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's more options on the table than just &quot;exacting formulae for every possible factor&quot; and &quot;just eyeball it,&quot; though. Just because Isator doesn't believe it will be the former doesn't mean it <i>has</i> to be the latter..</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of an excluded middle in that, yeah. I think advice on what effects are, when to use them, and also just how sometimes you want an effect that don't fit a simple dice trick, is likely going to be quite a bit of space there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T12:19:34-07:00","id":1316471,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking of the &quot;10m is Excalibur&quot; guidance and the artifact/manse creation rules from Oadenol's Codex might have been a better example than the magitech rules in Wonders.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure you really get the scope of the powers that can be created in the games I cited. I wouldn't have a problem creating any Evocation under either system.<br /> <br /> And yes, we're all expecting guidance in Exigents. We were also expecting guidance in Arms.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/572078-how-to-draw-an-owl\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/572/078/d6d.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/572078-how-to-draw-an-owl\" target=\"_blank\"> Original | How To Draw an Owl </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/572078-how-to-draw-an-owl\" target=\"_blank\"> https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/572078-how-to-draw-an-owl </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> See more 'How To Draw an Owl' images on Know Your Meme! </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-04-2019, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T12:40:25-07:00","id":1316472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316471#post1316471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, we're all expecting guidance in Exigents. We were also expecting guidance in Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Evocation design is identical to Charm design, so any Charm design guidance is directly applicable to Evocation design. Exigents is explicitly &quot;the guide to designing exalts and the lore of the Custom Exalt Splat&quot;.<br /> <br /> There was a dev change between when Arms are promised to have guidance to when it was actually written. In that downtime and from that dev switch, the concept of Evocations was expanded greatly, making the book much more full and leaving less room for guidance. It was disappointing for sure. Trust me, I'm the guy people asked to review custom Artifacts on these forums, so I was excited for something more official than my opinion. I won't argue that against wishing it had been in the book that it was promised for.<br /> <br /> But if Exigents doesn't have charm guidance, it'll be a very, very small book as that's much of the content right there. Unless there's another dev change between now and then, I propose giving them the benefit of the doubt that they'll deliver what they said they would. (Leaving aside the very real possibility that it'll deliver the letter of the promise if not the spirit extent to which individuals might prefer)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T12:49:21-07:00","id":1316476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316471#post1316471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking of the &quot;10m is Excalibur&quot; guidance and the artifact/manse creation rules from Oadenol's Codex might have been a better example than the magitech rules in Wonders.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure you really get the scope of the powers that can be created in the games I cited. I wouldn't have a problem creating any Evocation under either system.<br /> <br /> And yes, we're all expecting guidance in Exigents. We were also expecting guidance in Arms.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/572078-how-to-draw-an-owl\" target=\"_blank\">https://knowyourmeme.com/photos/5720...to-draw-an-owl</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is not designed to be a generic powers game. If it wanted to be, we would have something pretty different mechancially. There is as much a gamefeel goal with its design as there is its expression,a nd I think that the games you note, while good for their goals in those games, ultimately express different design philosophy of &quot;one size fits all&quot; powers versus more specific mechanica and exception-based design of Exalted 3e. Which is why citing them is pointless to me, as they are not even trying to be the same thing and the design goals of Evocations ended up not being this. Note, there was a point where Evocations did have a more menu-based system. That hasn't been the case since well before the corebook leaked, however.<br /> <br /> Arms as a note was, I think, not promised to have guiddance so much as examples. Anything to it having more mechanical details was based on earlier designs when Evocations worked on a much, much simpler system based on a menu of powers based on the Artifacts material. (This is why Arms origianllyw as less than 100 pages in its origianl solicitation.) What we ended up getting from the devs was actualyl <i>not</i> originally promised to my understanding in its current form, and we did get them nonetheless.<br /> <br /> We got the guidelines in effect that have been written for writers already. More in-depth general power design is better suited to be in one place all about homebrew power design, which is what Exigents is meant to do. Arms never was meant to be that and never to my understandings old as that beyond guidelines, which we do have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T15:13:03-07:00","id":1316501,"title":"","content":"The original outline for Arms of the Chosen (which we did not write) did not include <i>any </i>guidance on artifact creation or Evocation design. Their inclusion is something we did at the eleventh hour because we thought it would be valuable to communicate the frameworks we'd used in designing the current system of artifacts.<br /> <br /> Adding more expansive and rigorous guidance would've required further delaying an already-delayed book at a point in time when Third Edition had gone years without a release, so that wasn't a realistic option.<br /> <br /> The Charm design section of Exigents, for a variety of reasons, is not subject to any of the problems mentioned above, and has a benefit that Arms of the Chosen didn't, in that it gets to build on top of the Charm design document I drew up for Lunar Charm writers for Fangs at the Gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T15:59:36-07:00","id":1316512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316471#post1316471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking of the &quot;10m is Excalibur&quot; guidance and the artifact/manse creation rules from Oadenol's Codex might have been a better example than the magitech rules in Wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>That first guideline was not very useful, because Excalibur is not a measurement of anything, and even within Solar Charms the value of any given quantity of motes varied wildly.<br /> <br /> Going by Third Edition Solar Charm design? You're looking at something in which the benefits of a given dice trick differ <i>dramatically</i> between Abilities. The basis for that is something that can be explained, but it's not a simple explanation producing a formula into which you can slot different examples into.<br /> <br /> For manse creation, if you're talking about the point-build system then that is definitely not going to be how Exigents are created. An Exalt is going to be <i>far</i> more complicated than a manse, or even an Artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, we're all expecting guidance in Exigents. We were also expecting guidance in Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expecting it in Arms was silly, and it was a silly thing to cater to; the pitch of the book we were provided with was about expanding on Artifacts. <br /> <br /> It's a more reasonable thing to expect in Exigents because that's always been the essential purpose of the book, but I think expectations need to be managed. I do not think that it's ever going to be easy to make an Exalt, and homebrewing an Exigent seems likely to always be a challenge.<br /> <br /> Still, part of why they exist is <i>for</i> the homebrew crowd, the people who kept coming out with their custom Essence 6 Infernals. The premise of lots of varied and unique Exalted for small gods is interesting, but I don't think there's a simple way to implement it that is in keeping with the general depiction of the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T16:23:42-07:00","id":1316515,"title":"","content":"I don't think it does a bad job at helping you customise.<br /> <br /> For example, compare the evocation Phantom Cavalry Cavalcade to the old spirit charm Host of Spirits, they both serve the same function of magically conjuring minions during a fight. The difference is that with the former you're given the power in the context of an existing weapon and need to reskin it into Demon Soldier Procession or Ghost Pirate Mob while the latter didn't come with an aesthetic and you had to decide what it looked like for a particular spirit and if they had any specific limitations when using it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T21:04:57-07:00","id":1316552,"title":"","content":"I am some what perplexed that many here thinks that Arms of the Chosen did a fair job of helping me as a Game Master to create artifacts and evocations.<br /> <br /> I am usually not viewed as an idiot despite not being good at rpg-mechanics intuitively, and while I respect what Vance said above about the 11th hour and understand all of that as very good and very valid reasons for being so lacking in that aspect, the book absolutely does not help me much at all personally with creating artifact powers and evocations, as well as balancing the lv of them. It gives a collection of nice artifacts with nice well written lore and some cool evocations on them, but not enough for me, as I am a much better story teller and writer than mechanics-engineer, to create my own evocations with any sort of ease. I love every book Vance and Minton have written, but Arms of the Chosen is the one I love the least by far. In fact, without having read Unsung Hero's guide, I would probably never have created one of my own, and even that artifact, I am hardly sure if is balanced or not (will post it on this forum for review by you experts when me and my player have it hundred percent done, since I apparently suck so hard at this ). Never the less, Unsung Hero is my personal hero when it comes to artifact creation as he has been of far greater help to me at least, so imo he/she is worthy of a few songs.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I much prefer having artifacts and evocations created for me as Game Master, so I can concentrate on knowing the rules and weaving my stories, so I personally would obviously like a Volume 2 of Arms with more artifacts and evocations as I found them too few (my player wanted an artifact Serpent-Sting-Staff specifically and there is no such thing in any Exalted book yet written, so we had to create one, which for sure has been fun, but also incredibly time consuming, and well, it is not done yet). But the way Exalted 3 is written, I don't have a choice I guess, which again, is fine since the game is so wonderfully awesome when it comes to the setting that it makes up for the annoying fact that I am expected to create my own artifacts and evocations with only cursory explanation as to how I should do that.<br /> But who knows, maybe this artifact creation process thing will grow on me as I become more accustomed to it. It might, as only time will tell. But for now I find it all very difficult. Therefore, it is very, very likely that people will see me posting a custom made artifact, desperately asking kindly for balance advice on evocations, in the near future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 06-05-2019, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T23:43:42-07:00","id":1316564,"title":"","content":"What Fire Has Wrought and Fangs at the Gate both have about a dozen Artifacts in them. As well as several Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I think we're going to get examples of both of those things basically anywhere that they can plausibly go.<br /> <br /> Oh, and spells!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:14:14-07:00","id":1316573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=897958#post897958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just finished listening to the podcast interview with John and Holden, it appears that Arms of the Chosen WILL have &amp;quot;more guidance and support for homebrewers than possibly any supplement ever before in Exalted&amp;quot; if I'm quoting that correctly. No idea what extent that is, but that's a very different direction than has been suggested earlier in this thread. So yay!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/880344-thought-about-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1316501#post1316501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original outline for Arms of the Chosen (which we did not write) did not include <i>any </i>guidance on artifact creation or Evocation design. Their inclusion is something we did at the eleventh hour because we thought it would be valuable to communicate the frameworks we'd used in designing the current system of artifacts.<br /> <br /> Adding more expansive and rigorous guidance would've required further delaying an already-delayed book at a point in time when Third Edition had gone years without a release, so that wasn't a realistic option.<br /> <br /> The Charm design section of Exigents, for a variety of reasons, is not subject to any of the problems mentioned above, and has a benefit that Arms of the Chosen didn't, in that it gets to build on top of the Charm design document I drew up for Lunar Charm writers for Fangs at the Gate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance, thank you for your candour. I eagerly await the Exigents book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:17:55-07:00","id":1316574,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Vance said Exigents will only have one artefact in it. But then, the point of the book is to help you homebrew.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, no Exalted book ever has had good rules for homebrewing, and now artefacts are way more complex than past editions, making a guide to homebrewing them also way more complex. I'm a bit sceptical that Exigents can do it well, but then, they are going to have way more word-count on it than I've seen before.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Isator is right, as Dragonblood was full of jade artefacts and Lunars was full of moonsilver ones, I'm sure Sidereals will have a bunch of starmetal artefacts and Abyssals will have a load of soulsteel ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}